WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:04.480
Christmas is a time of comfort, joy, and cocoa
by the tree.

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:09.080
But if you're in the right kind of mood, it's
also a time for killer Santas, demonic elves,

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.600
and other seasonal frights.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:15.580
If you want to curl up by the fire for a monstrous
movie marathon, here are the best and worst

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.920
films out there for your yuletide slay.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.580
Black Christmas is the twisted godmother of
holiday horror films.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.900
The plot is a familiar one, with a mysterious
killer picking off victims in a sorority house

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:26.840
around Christmas.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:31.960
But more than four decades after its release,
this wintery slasher still wins over viewers

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.560
with its haunting holiday tone.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:38.720
The film features terrifying murder sequences,
compelling performances, and one of the most

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:43.740
unsettling phone calls in horror movie history
- all set against a cozy Christmas backdrop.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.880
"Just like having a wart removed!”

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:51.580
“Oh my god."

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:56.920
Nearly a decade later, director Bob Clark
did a complete turnaround with a very different

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:00.400
holiday classic - the slightly-less violent
A Christmas Story.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.620
Now that's a double feature.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.200
"You'll shoot your eye out, you’ll shoot
your eye out!

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.860
Hahaha!”

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:12.960
It's no surprise that Black Christmas got
the extreme remake treatment.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.360
But louder, gorier, and darker doesn't necessarily
equal better.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:22.750
Released in 2006, this second incarnation
attempted to flesh out exactly what was behind

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:27.610
the brutal murders at the sorority house,
and while the answer to that mystery is satisfyingly

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:31.060
bizarre, it does pull time away from the victims
and their stories.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:35.260
Aside from spelling out the killer's origins,
the remake attempts to distinguish itself

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.820
through increasingly disgusting murder sequences.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:41.840
But it's all just soulless violence, with
little charm or fun to be found.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.329
For all its effort to grow its mythology and
serve up twisted kill scenes, the end result

00:01:46.329 --> 00:01:48.260
is both too much, and not enough.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:52.500
There are plenty of Christmas movies that
explore the mythology of Santa Claus, each

00:01:52.509 --> 00:01:54.579
one hoping to add something to the legend.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.620
Few films really succeed at this.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:02:01.500
One exception is Rare Exports, a Finnish film
that offers a fascinating, creepy new take

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.680
on Father Christmas.

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:06.320
Perhaps the best thing about the film is the
way it plays with the tropes of Christmas

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:06.820
movies.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:11.320
There's a struggling family, a boy searching
for a reason to believe in magic, and some

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:16.000
wonderful supernatural happenings, all twisted
into a frightening fantasy tale.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:21.060
It's a film that both celebrates and subverts
Christmas, shattering the illusions its characters

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.920
have about the holiday as the dark truth about
Santa Claus is unearthed.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:29.260
For at least one Christmas Eve, you'll be
thinking about Saint Nick very differently.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.600
You probably don't want to let that guy in
your house.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:37.200
Silent Night, Deadly Night is a campy slasher
classic with one of the best posters in horror

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:37.700
history.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:42.640
But its sequel is mostly a dull retread of
the first film, and is about as much fun as

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:43.640
a lump of coal.

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:48.920
Thanks to a flimsy framing device, the movie
spends a huge chunk of its runtime on flashbacks.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:52.720
As a result, a whole lot of footage from the
first movie is reused.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:57.340
By the time the film gets around to new material,
you're bored enough to turn it off.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.080
You may as well stick with the original.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:02.500
Or press pause on the horror movies, and go
spend time with your family.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.360
"Why would I want to do that?"

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:09.500
If you're looking for the creepiest film about
a killer Santa, then seek out Christmas Evil.

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:13.760
It's the story of a man whose perception of
Saint Nick was forever warped by a childhood

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:14.260
incident.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:18.400
leaving him feeling responsible for keeping
the spirit of Christmas alive himself.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:23.860
That warped vision ultimately makes him want
to be Santa, keeping tabs on local children

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:27.620
- which, despite Santa's example, is an insanely
scary thing to do.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:31.720
It all leads up to a murder spree that plays
out in a way that's much less campy than you

00:03:31.721 --> 00:03:32.730
might expect.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:37.060
Forget the reason for the season - this is
just a bona fide horror film, with a desire

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:39.880
to truly scare that makes it an underseen
gem.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:44.460
"Your name goes in the bad boys and girls
book.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:49.460
And i’ll bring you something... horrible."

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:53.100
Jack Frost is not, by traditional standards,
a good movie.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:57.940
It's the story of a serial killer whose DNA
merges with snow after the truck taking him

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:00.580
to be executed crashes into some toxic goo.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:05.540
He then takes the form of a sentient, shapeshifting
snowman, who terrorizes a small town with

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:07.200
his crappy visual effects.

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:13.260
Despite failing with both critics and audiences,
Jack Frost has stuck around since its 1997

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.540
release, seeming blissfully unaware of just
how bad it is.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:20.380
Do you want a holiday movie with a bit of
spooky flair that won't scar the kids for

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:20.880
life?

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:21.920
Then watch Gremlins.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:26.540
Joe Dante's classic about a boy and his strange
pet Christmas present has been a source of

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.560
imaginative fun for thirty years.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:33.900
Every '80s kid knows you can't feed a mogwai
after midnight - even if Gremlins 2 admits

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.500
that rule doesn't really make sense.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:36.920
“Well wait a minute, what about this?

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:40.220
What if they’re eating in an airplane, and
they cross a time zone?

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:41.780
I mean, it’s always midnight somewhere.”

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:49.320
Santa's Slay might be a bad movie, but it's
hard to watch without having a good time.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:54.040
Famously starring professional wrestler Bill
Goldberg, the film goes all-in on its premise

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.400
of a murderous Santa.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:05:00.320
And this is no mere imitator - this is the
real deal Kris Kringle, coming straight out

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:01.160
of the depths of Hell.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:06.400
Santa's sleigh is pulled by demonic reindeer,
and he keeps things brutally on-brand, taking

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:09.480
out all of his victims in a seasonally appropriate
way.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:14.280
This villainous Saint Nicholas isn't just
a Santa gone mad - he's a Santa born bad.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:18.440
It's so stupid that it's awesome - but it's
still really, really stupid.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:22.610
The internet's favorite Christmas monster
has a movie well worth watching.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:26.960
Krampus starts as the story of a dysfunctional
family coming together for a tense holiday

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:31.180
reunion, with one side being uptight, and
the other being a little gun-crazy.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:36.130
When one of the kids loses the Christmas spirit
and shreds his letter to Santa, things quickly

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:37.260
take a chilling turn.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:41.740
A blizzard sets in and the power goes out,
leaving the family waiting for a visit not

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:44.340
from Santa, but rather his dark shadow.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:49.500
Well made and delightfully feisty, Krampus
is a creature feature for all seasons, a work

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:52.020
of horror comedy that just works on every
level.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:55.200
Enough murderous Santas - how about a killer
elf?

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:59.900
Most of this horror unfolds at a department
store, where a group of teenagers and an ex-cop

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:02.360
Santa impersonator are spending the night.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:07.360
It turns out they aren't alone, because a
strange elf creature is also roaming around,

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:08.080
raising hell.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.040
"They have magical powers, they can’t be
hurt or killed.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:12.040
They eat anything.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:13.440
They’re a perfect soldier."

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:17.620
That sounds like an okay premise, but Elves
gets so much stranger.

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:22.170
The Dan Haggerty-starring movie is so bad,
with a story so bonkers, that it's actually

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:22.860
kind of good.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:26.820
What do Santa's little helpers have in common
with a secret Nazi plot?

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:28.500
It's way more than you'd expect.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:31.640
You'll have to see it to believe it - but
you just might wish you hadn't.

